    "b-10-purpose-the-kernel-is-designed-f-5": {
      "id": "b-10-purpose-the-kernel-is-designed-f-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The kernel is designed for agent systems that are extraordinarily token-hungry. A workload that spins up, say, 64 parallel workers can spend thousands of dollars in minutes. In that regime, cost is the dominant engineering risk: if you cannot see where tokens are going and measure the effectiveness behind each spend, you have no way to make the system sustainable."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-purpose-this-is-why-observabilit-6": {
      "id": "b-10-purpose-this-is-why-observabilit-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "This is why observability and control are not secondary features. They are the reason the kernel exists. The product of an agent system is not just the work it does: it is "
        },
        {
          "insert": "viewable",
          "attributes": {
            "italic": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " agent execution that you can attribute, budget, and improve."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
